      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The answer is in [[credential-scoping]]. \n\nThe Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by **never holding it there in the first place**. Instead:\n\n1. **A local secrets loader** reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup.\n2. **The key is injected only into child processes** \u2014 specifically into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent (and Query agent) child process, immediately before that process starts.\n3. **The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated** \u2014 it never contains the credential.\n\nThis architecture means that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, an attacker cannot leak the API key simply by inspecting the Hub\u0027s environment variables. The credential exists only inside the short-lived child processes that actually need it to call the Anthropic API.",
      "input_tokens": 5314,
      "output_tokens": 193
    }
